The owner asked for UI design research on how to build the best search bar control (with results) that fits our workflow — the planner's search-and-star picker (`plan/plan.js` + `plan/lib/search.js`) — delivered as a behaviourally detailed design doc, explicitly **without** implementing the control yet.

Deliverable: `plan/design/SEARCH_BAR_DESIGN.md` —

- a survey of the published search-UX guidance (Baymard autocomplete patterns, NN/g site-search suggestions and scoped search, WAI-ARIA combobox pattern, multi-select combobox field findings, typo-tolerance / zero-results practice), each mapped to a keep-or-change verdict for our control;
- an audit of today's behaviour, promoted to spec where it's already right;
- the target behavioural specification (open/close state table, keyboard and pointer models, match highlighting, bounded typo tolerance, zero-result culprit naming, ARIA corrections);
- a prioritised P1–P3 implementation queue for follow-up work and open questions for the owner.

Follow-up implementation work is out of scope here and should be tracked per queue item once the doc's recommendations are agreed.

